  "slug": "pangenome-reference-d002",
  "summary": "Preprints report GPU, quantum and reproducibility-focused implementations of haplotype and variant inference on sequencing and single-cell atlas data.",
  "synthesis": "The four preprints share a computational focus on inferring genomic state from sequencing or single-cell data rather than a common reference framework. Phirefly performs hierarchical read-based haplotype phasing at chromosome scale, with key steps run on quantum hardware and accuracy reported as comparable to QHap and mainstream approaches. BRISANCE applies a GPU-accelerated Parabricks pipeline to somatic short-variant detection in HG008 tumor-normal WGS, reporting 73.66% overlap with DRAGEN and a 20.6-fold runtime improvement. CyteArc analyzes remote single-cell atlases in place at about 100 million cells, with provenance tracking. The Fusion transpiler study tests whether SNHA network-inference code remains functionally identical across nine languages. What is new is the emphasis on implementation: hardware acceleration, scale and cross-language reproducibility are evaluated alongside inference accuracy.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
